{"title":"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 41","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_41\">Problem 41</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_41&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 41\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A train traveling from Aytown to Beetown meets with an accident after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hr. It is stopped for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> hr., \nafter which it proceeds at four-fifths of its usual rate, arriving at Beetown <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hr. late. \nIf the train had covered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles more before the accident, it would have been just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hr. late. \nThe usual rate of the train is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7a482aad0623d908c20d1e7b79c066eda6d46b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{20 mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{30 mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{40 mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{50 mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{60 mph}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"575\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_41&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the usual speed of the train in miles per hour, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the total distance from Aytown to Beetown, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a91531c8228d8092c2d87ea2535a84ba02cbfc20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = \\frac{d}{v}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"53\" height=\"39\" /> be the normal travel time in hours.\n</p><p><b>Scenario 1:</b>\nThe train travels at speed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour, stops for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> hour, and covers the remaining distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7c3e31626bc0dba6cc8d91ef361f9ce7a6ae74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d - v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> at speed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92cfe32f18d8a6e0c66ef4c2a84b7ae4503c689d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5}v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />. Since the train arrives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours late, the total time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7acf867039824c715b06177534297c9dbbe10035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/961346480d827bd6e0be78b2dc169452e135c134.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{d - v}{\\frac{4}{5}v} = T + 2\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc0e9513a7475b679a6d5171630952fcc17ca2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d - v}{v} = \\frac{d}{v} - 1 = T - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"185\" height=\"39\" />, we substitute this into the equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/6415e323f380a8f9b6fee7f2244221b6bf0770e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{5}{4}(T - 1) = T + 2\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f4f7fa1c7ddea50d4fffaeba8c0d9ef8451d9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{5}{4}T - \\frac{5}{4} = T + 2\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/86157aa193a104ef3d21fb0d7d7cbabb20dd7a75.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{5}{4}T = T + 2\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43eb37f0b46cf2f5b70be5b27db15aa7149878bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{4}T = \\frac{7}{4} \\implies T = 7 \\text{ hours}\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><b>Scenario 2:</b>\nIf the accident had occurred <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles further, the train would have traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94a4b8c5938e4a0617f5d0e29c7c45258cc2c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + \\frac{80}{v}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" /> hours at normal speed before the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> hour delay. The remaining distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d9a13d62fdead11980e37a90530a8e7965c3868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d - v - 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> is then covered at speed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92cfe32f18d8a6e0c66ef4c2a84b7ae4503c689d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5}v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />. Since the train is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour late, the total time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a1465964de056c550f2f656e938a24510f3d9e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/795d459bba100c38585263db74577a688704df33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(1 + \\frac{80}{v}\\right) + \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{d - v - 80}{\\frac{4}{5}v} = T + 1\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>We can rewrite the remaining distance term using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/07253879861ff215773eb9bb7bda52eed5e77972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d - v}{v} = T - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"39\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa928fc68cdd94041994d49ca737fde49568fa0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{80}{v} + \\frac{5}{4}\\left(T - 1 - \\frac{80}{v}\\right) = T + 1\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Expanding the terms gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a0c0a80ca90c7ba44b604a1bb75ee194fdaf4cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{80}{v} + \\frac{5}{4}(T - 1) - \\frac{100}{v} = T + 1\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12ed85310c42e4e49d301a766d01facf45299e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = 7$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded813775cf6b709bdbe7592d08938c5e951d93e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{80}{v} + \\frac{5}{4}(6) - \\frac{100}{v} = 8\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/190ce7b8f2178939bbb62574eb4566bb9f78ed8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{15}{2} - \\frac{20}{v} = 8\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c708092b9590cc4fe220829dd87d4784f43a1f93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9 - \\frac{20}{v} = 8\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/23921085ec2ee3e996631aff7e2681fa2588eef6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{20}{v} = 1 \\implies v = 20\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the usual rate of the train is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad3c0a70af3642ff8b9db5e722a6188cc70f52d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{20 \\text{ mph}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, which corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5bdc2c0e59651ee5e6fa74ba318dc73d744feb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_41&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME\" title=\"1955 AHSME\">1955 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1955 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1955\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 40\">Problem 40</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_42\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 42\">Problem 42</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=